  #set text(font: "Palatino Linotype", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(166.49pt, 102.26pt, "1.1. Challenges in Current Detection Methods ")
  #set text(font: "Palatino Linotype", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(187.73pt, 118.1pt, "A diverse range of methods and tools has been explored, encompassing sensor-based ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 130.94pt, "real-time monitoring technologies [7], advanced data analysis approaches [8], and visual ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 143.66pt, "inspection techniques [9]. Despite these advancements, there remain significant chal-")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 156.5pt, "lenges and gaps: ")
  #line-at(187.73pt, 169.34pt, "Sensor Deployment and Data Management: Han and Yang [10] noted the challenges ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 182.18pt, "in installing sensors effectively for continuous monitoring. The difficulty lies not only in ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 195.02pt, "the installation but also in maintaining these sensors and managing the vast amounts of ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 207.74pt, "data they generate, especially in harsh and remote environments where wind turbines are ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 220.58pt, "typically located. ")
  #line-at(187.73pt, 233.42pt, "Efficient Data Analysis: Zhang et al. [11] proposed a method using mechanical vibra-")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 246.26pt, "tions, reducing the number of samples needed for effective conclusions by 60%. However, ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 259.1pt, "the variability in turbine models and operational environments means that the analysis ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 271.85pt, "needs to be robust across different conditions, which remains a challenge. Han et al. [12] ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 284.69pt, "addressed the scarcity of samples for deep learning, proposing a semi-supervised fault ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 297.53pt, "diagnosis model that works efficiently with few samples, yet the model’s accuracy under ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 310.37pt, "different conditions still requires further validation. In addition, Wang et al. [13] proposed ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 323.21pt, "a graph attention autoencoder for blade icing supervision, which utilizes sensor data from ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 335.93pt, "supervisory control and data acquisition (SCADA) systems. This method shows promise ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 348.77pt, "but requires further testing under various operational conditions to fully validate its ef-")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 361.61pt, "fectiveness. ")
  #line-at(187.73pt, 374.45pt, "Visual Inspection Innovations: Visual inspection methods, including UAV-based ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 387.29pt, "techniques, have advanced significantly. Guo et al. [14] and Bernalte and García [15] uti-")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 400.01pt, "lized UAVs and image analysis for fault detection, highlighting the potential of these ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 412.85pt, "methods. However, automating these inspections to reduce human error and ensuring ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 425.69pt, "consistent accuracy in various environmental conditions are ongoing issues. ")
  #line-at(187.73pt, 438.53pt, "Integration of Acoustic and Vibration Signals: Liu and Zhang [16], Li et al. [17], and ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 451.39pt, "Wang et al. [18] proposed combining acoustic emission with vibration signals for detect-")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 464.11pt, "ing cracks and other faults. Although promising, these methods require more research to ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 476.95pt, "integrate effectively into comprehensive fault detection systems that can operate reliably ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 489.79pt, "in real-world scenarios. ")
  #line-at(187.73pt, 502.63pt, "Machine Learning in Fault Detection: Machine learning has shown significant poten-")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 515.47pt, "tial, particularly in processing large datasets from SCADA systems. Banala et al. [19] used ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 528.19pt, "machine learning for real-time monitoring, and Ogaili et al. [20] proposed an ARIMA ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 541.03pt, "model for predictive analysis. Additionally, Rangel et al. [21] integrated convolutional ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 553.87pt, "neural networks (CNNs) and frequency–time analysis to detect 62 blade faults with 100% ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 566.71pt, "accuracy for unbalanced and bearing faults. Gajbhiye and Warudkar [22] further empha-")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 579.55pt, "sized the benefits of CNNs in wind turbine blade failure detection, showing that these ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 592.39pt, "networks reduce the need for human intervention and lower costs. However, these meth-")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 605.11pt, "ods are often data-hungry and computationally intensive, which can be limiting factors in ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 617.98pt, "their widespread adoption. ")
  #set text(font: "Palatino Linotype", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(166.49pt, 642.82pt, "1.2. Importance of Energy Efficiency and Sustainability ")
  #set text(font: "Palatino Linotype", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(187.73pt, 658.66pt, "The relationship between energy efficiency and fault detection in wind turbine blades ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 671.5pt, "is well established. Wang et al. [23] demonstrated that predictive maintenance could en-")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 684.22pt, "hance energy efficiency by reducing downtime and preventing catastrophic failures. ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 697.06pt, "Zhang et al. [24] used statistical data from offshore wind farms to show that fault detection ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 709.9pt, "could improve energy efficiency, using methods like Fuzzy Fault Tree Analysis to assess ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 722.74pt, "risks. ")
  #line-at(187.73pt, 735.58pt, "Machine learning, particularly artificial intelligence, has emerged as a crucial tool for ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 748.296pt, "fault detection, as exemplified by Mourad et al. [25], who analyzed wind turbines using ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 761.136pt, "SCADA data. They implemented a Gaussian mixture model, yielding accurate results in ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 773.976pt, "predicting and locating faults. Du et al. [26] proposed, based on data obtained from a ")
]

