  #set text(font: "Palatino Linotype", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(166.49pt, 490.75pt, "2.1. Data Mining ")
  #set text(font: "Palatino Linotype", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(187.73pt, 506.59pt, "The types of supervised machine learning are regression, in which the target variable ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 519.43pt, "is continuous, and classification, in which the target variable is categorical. The following ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 532.27pt, "is required to build a classification model: characteristics that can be quantified, a labeled ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 544.99pt, "target or outcome variable, and a method for measuring similarity. ")
  #line-at(187.73pt, 557.83pt, "A linear regression models the relationship between a continuous variable and one ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 570.67pt, "or more scaling variables, usually represented as a dependent function equal to the sum ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 583.51pt, "of a coefficient plus the scaling factors multiplied by the independent variables. Residuals ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 596.35pt, "are defined as the difference between an actual value and a predicted value; a recom-")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 609.07pt, "mended modeling practice for linear regression is as follows: use the cost function to fit ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 621.94pt, "the linear regression model; develop multiple models; and compare the results and choose ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 634.78pt, "the one that fits the data and whether it is using the model for prediction or interpretation. ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 647.62pt, "Three standard measures of error for linear regressions are the sum of squared errors ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 660.46pt, "(")
  #set text(font: "Palatino Linotype", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(169.85pt, 660.46pt, "SSE")
  #set text(font: "Palatino Linotype", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(187.01pt, 660.46pt, "), sum total of squares (")
  #set text(font: "Palatino Linotype", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(290.35pt, 660.46pt, "SST")
  #set text(font: "Palatino Linotype", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(307.51pt, 660.46pt, "), and coefficient of determination (")
  #set text(font: "Palatino Linotype", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(462.94pt, 660.46pt, "R")
  #set text(font: "Palatino Linotype", size: 6pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(469.54pt, 657.94pt, "2")
  #set text(font: "Palatino Linotype", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(472.54pt, 660.46pt, "). ")
  #line-at(187.73pt, 673.18pt, "Unsupervised learning is a machine learning technique in which models analyze un-")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 686.02pt, "labeled data to find hidden patterns, relationships, and structures. Unlike supervised ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 698.86pt, "learning, where correct answers are provided, unsupervised learning has no human in-")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 711.7pt, "tervention to guide the process. The models discover connections and patterns on their ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 724.54pt, "own from the available data [36–39]. ")
  #line-at(187.73pt, 737.26pt, "In the context of unsupervised learning, algorithms are employed to cluster unla-")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 750.096pt, "beled datasets based on their similarities or differences. Some of the more commonly em-")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 762.936pt, "ployed approaches include clustering. One of the principal objectives of unsupervised ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 775.776pt, "learning is the process of clustering. Clustering techniques are employed to group ")
]

