  #line-at(187.73pt, 267.89pt, "Finally, neural networks are a class of machine learning models inspired by the struc-")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 280.73pt, "ture and function of biological neurons. These models are particularly powerful in cap-")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 293.45pt, "turing complex, non-linear relationships between inputs and outputs, making them ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 306.29pt, "highly suitable for a wide range of predictive tasks [49]. The architecture of a neural net-")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 319.13pt, "work consists of interconnected layers of artificial neurons, typically organized into an ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 331.97pt, "input layer, one or more hidden layers, and an output layer. ")
  #line-at(187.73pt, 344.81pt, "The output of each neuron in a layer is computed as a weighted sum of its inputs, ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 357.53pt, "followed by the application of an activation function. Mathematically, for a given neuron ")
  #set text(font: "Palatino Linotype", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(166.49pt, 371.69pt, "j ")
