  #line-at(187.73pt, 684.82pt, "To determine which neural network model fits best for a particular task, one must ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 697.54pt, "evaluate several architectures and hyperparameter configurations. Key factors to consider ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 710.38pt, "include the number of hidden layers, the number of neurons per layer, the choice of acti-")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 723.22pt, "vation functions, and the regularization techniques (e.g., dropout, L2 regularization) to ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 736.06pt, "prevent overfitting. ")
  #line-at(187.73pt, 748.896pt, "Model selection can be systematically approached by dividing the dataset into train-")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 761.736pt, "ing, validation, and test sets. The training set is used to fit the model, the validation set is ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 774.456pt, "used to tune hyperparameters and select the best model, and the test set provides an ")
]

// arXiv source page 11
#original-page(595.32pt, 841.92pt, (image("graphics/page-11.png", width: 526.5pt), 34.5pt, 67.5pt))[
  #set text(font: "Palatino Linotype", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(36pt, 59.4pt, "Appl. Sci. ")
  #set text(font: "Palatino Linotype", size: 8.04pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(69.984pt, 59.4pt, "2024")
  #set text(font: "Palatino Linotype", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(86.064pt, 59.4pt, ",")
  #set text(font: "Palatino Linotype", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(87.984pt, 59.4pt, " 14")
  #set text(font: "Palatino Linotype", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(98.064pt, 59.4pt, ", x FOR PEER REVIEW ")
  #line-at(528.36pt, 59.4pt, "11 of 21 ")
  #set text(font: "Palatino Linotype", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(166.49pt, 102.26pt, "unbiased evaluation of the model’s performance. Cross-validation techniques can further ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 115.1pt, "enhance the robustness of model selection by averaging performance metrics over multi-")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 127.94pt, "ple folds of the data. ")
  #line-at(187.73pt, 140.66pt, "Finally, metrics such as accuracy, precision, recall, F1-score, or mean squared error ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 153.5pt, "(depending on the task) are used to compare the performance of different models. The ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 166.34pt, "model with the best performance on the validation or test set is considered the best fit for ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 179.18pt, "the given problem. ")
  #line-at(187.73pt, 192.02pt, "The models employed by Orange Data Mining utilize a neural network to ascertain ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 204.74pt, "the optimal model, with the logistic regression widget selected to facilitate this determi-")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 217.58pt, "nation. The tree algorithm is a straightforward approach that partitions the data into ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 230.42pt, "nodes based on class purity (information gain for categorical and MSE for numeric target ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 243.26pt, "variables). The Tree widget, designed in-house, is capable of handling both categorical ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 256.1pt, "and numeric datasets. The Neural Network widget utilizes the sklearn Multi-layer Per-")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 268.85pt, "ceptron algorithm, which is capable of learning both non-linear and linear models. Naive ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 281.69pt, "Bayes is a fast and simple probabilistic classifier based on Bayes’ theorem, assuming fea-")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 294.53pt, "ture independence. Subsequently, the confusion matrix provides the number or propor-")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 307.37pt, "tion of instances between the predicted and actual class. The selection of elements from ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 320.21pt, "the matrix is then fed into the corresponding instances of the output signal. This allows ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 332.93pt, "the user to identify which instances were misclassified and how. Subsequently, an image ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 345.77pt, "viewer is incorporated to facilitate observation of the algorithmic identification of images ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 358.61pt, "exhibiting defects, as illustrated in Figure 5. ")
  #set text(font: "Palatino Linotype", size: 9pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(166.49pt, 599.23pt, "Figure 5. ")
  #set text(font: "Palatino Linotype", size: 9pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(204.29pt, 599.23pt, "Final setup for detecting defects in wind turbine blades. ")
  #set text(font: "Palatino Linotype", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(166.49pt, 623.74pt, "2.4. Clustering ")
  #set text(font: "Palatino Linotype", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(187.73pt, 639.58pt, "According to Yang et al. [30], deep image clustering networks can categorize unla-")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 652.42pt, "beled images, and Orange Data Mining associates the images with their distances. In this ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 665.26pt, "case, the Distances widget computes distances between rows or columns in a dataset. The ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 677.98pt, "data will be normalized by default to ensure equal treatment of individual features. Nor-")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 690.82pt, "malization is always done column-wise. To visualize the computed clusters, an Image ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 703.66pt, "Viewer widget is added. A Hierarchical Clustering widget is used for the hierarchical al-")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 716.5pt, "gorithm. The complete clustering diagram can be seen in Figure 6. ")
]

