  #line-at(187.73pt, 201.74pt, "As illustrated in Table 3, the logistic regression model exhibits the highest AUC value ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 214.58pt, "(0.791), thereby indicating its superior overall capacity to discriminate between the vari-")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 227.42pt, "ous classes. The neural network exhibits a second-best AUC (0.740), yet this value is mark-")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 240.14pt, "edly inferior to that of the logistic regression model. The performance of the tree and naive ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 252.98pt, "Bayes models in terms of AUC indicates that they are less effective at distinguishing be-")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 265.85pt, "tween the classes. Table 4 reveals that tree exhibits the highest classification accuracy ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 278.69pt, "(0.893), indicating that it is the most effective at correctly classifying instances. Moderate ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 291.53pt, "accuracies are observed for the neural network (0.561) and logistic regression (0.474). Con-")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 304.25pt, "versely, naive Bayes has the lowest accuracy (0.107), suggesting poor performance in clas-")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 317.09pt, "sifying data correctly. Table 5 reveals that the neural network has the highest F1-score ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 329.93pt, "(0.795), indicating an optimal balance between precision and recall. Logistic regression ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 342.77pt, "and tree also demonstrate satisfactory performance (0.665 and 0.520, respectively), ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 355.61pt, "whereas naive Bayes exhibits the lowest F1-score (0.174), suggesting suboptimal precision ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 368.33pt, "and recall balancing. Table 6 reveals that the neural network has the highest precision ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 381.17pt, "(0.741), indicating an ability to minimize false positives. Logistic regression also performs ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 394.01pt, "well with a precision of 0.525, while naive Bayes and tree demonstrate lower precision ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 406.85pt, "values, with naive Bayes exhibiting the lowest precision (0.292). Table 7 reveals that tree ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 419.69pt, "has the highest recall (0.893), indicating its effectiveness in identifying all relevant in-")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 432.53pt, "stances. The neural network and logistic regression also demonstrate high recall scores, ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 445.27pt, "although not as high as that of tree. Conversely, naive Bayes exhibits a notably low recall ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 458.11pt, "(0.200), suggesting a tendency to overlook relevant instances. Table 8 reveals that the neu-")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 470.95pt, "ral network exhibits the highest specificity (0.767), indicating its efficacy in identifying ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 483.79pt, "negative instances. Both tree and logistic regression demonstrate satisfactory performance ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 496.63pt, "with specificity values of 0.681 and 0.319, respectively. Conversely, naive Bayes exhibits ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 509.35pt, "lower specificity values, suggesting its diminished capacity in identifying non-relevant ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 522.19pt, "instances. Finally, Table 9 reveals that the neural network and logistic regression models ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 535.03pt, "exhibit the lowest logistic loss values, indicating superior performance in terms of mini-")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 547.87pt, "mizing prediction error. In contrast, the tree and naive Bayes models demonstrate higher ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 560.71pt, "logistic loss, suggesting inferior performance in this regard. ")
  #line-at(187.73pt, 573.43pt, "Logistic regression excels in AUC and shows competitive results in F1-score, preci-")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 586.27pt, "sion, and recall, making it a strong overall model. The neural network performs well in ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 599.11pt, "AUC, F1-score, precision, and specificity but struggles with classification accuracy and ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 611.95pt, "logistic loss. Tree shows high classification accuracy and recall but is weaker in AUC, pre-")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 624.82pt, "cision, and logistic loss. Naive Bayes generally performs poorly across most metrics, in-")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 637.54pt, "cluding AUC, classification accuracy, precision, recall, and specificity. ")
  #line-at(187.73pt, 650.38pt, "Overall, logistic regression appears to be the most balanced model, offering strong ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 663.22pt, "performance across multiple metrics, while the neural network and tree have their own ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 676.06pt, "strengths and weaknesses. Naive Bayes is consistently the least effective across the board. ")
  #line-at(187.73pt, 688.9pt, "The confusion matrix gives the number or proportion of instances between the pre-")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 701.62pt, "dicted and actual class. The selection of the elements in the matrix feeds the corresponding ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 714.46pt, "instances into the output signal. This way, one can observe which specific instances were ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 727.3pt, "misclassified and how. Figure 7 presents the confusion matrices of the neural network, ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 740.14pt, "tree, logistic regression, and naive Bayes models. ")
]

