  #line-at(166.49pt, 393.29pt, "fusion matrices, different colors are often used to make interpretation easier: Blue often ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 406.01pt, "used to highlight correct predictions (True Positive and True Negative); Red or Orange ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 418.85pt, "often used for incorrect predictions (False Positive and False Negative). Sometimes, the ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 431.69pt, "intensity of the color indicates the magnitude of the values, with darker shades represent-")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 444.55pt, "ing higher numbers. Each confusion matrix illustrates the performance of these models in ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 457.39pt, "predicting categories labeled as “Blade 1”, “Blade 2”, and “Blade 3”. ")
  #line-at(187.73pt, 470.11pt, "Confusion Matrices Overview: Rows (Actual): Represent the true classes; Columns ")
