  #set text(font: "Palatino Linotype", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(166.49pt, 316.13pt, "3.2. Image Clustering ")
  #set text(font: "Palatino Linotype", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(187.73pt, 331.97pt, "Once the image embedding was performed, the Distances tool was used, and the re-")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 344.81pt, "sulting distance matrix could be fed further into hierarchical clustering to uncover groups ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 357.65pt, "in the data.  ")
  #line-at(187.73pt, 370.49pt, "The result of the hierarchical clustering is presented in Figure 9. ")
  #set text(font: "Palatino Linotype", size: 9pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(166.49pt, 580.39pt, "Figure 9. ")
  #set text(font: "Palatino Linotype", size: 9pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(204.41pt, 580.39pt, "Hierarchical clustering of wind blade images. ")
  #set text(font: "Palatino Linotype", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(187.73pt, 604.87pt, "Figure 9 shows the results of a hierarchical clustering analysis applied to a set of im-")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 617.74pt, "ages of wind turbine blades with defects. The horizontal axis represents the distance or ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 630.46pt, "dissimilarity between clusters as they merge. A higher value indicates a greater difference ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 643.3pt, "between clusters before they are combined. The vertical axis displays the names of the ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 656.14pt, "blade images. The images are grouped into different branches, where each branch fusion ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 668.98pt, "represents the combination of two clusters into one. Mergers occur from individual ele-")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 681.82pt, "ments (the images) to the final cluster that contains all the data. ")
  #line-at(187.73pt, 694.54pt, "By observing Figure 9, there are some well-defined groups, such as the images “Blade ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 707.38pt, "3/Blade 5.jpg” and “Blade 3/Blade 4.jpg,” which are clustered very closely together, indi-")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 720.22pt, "cating they are like each other based on the characteristics considered in the analysis. ")
  #line-at(187.73pt, 733.06pt, "The image labels are colored, which may indicate different predefined categories or ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 745.896pt, "subgroups of blades (perhaps based on defect type or blade location). ")
  #line-at(187.73pt, 758.736pt, "By examining the structure of the branches, the groups of images with similar colors ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 771.456pt, "tend to cluster together, suggesting that the images within the same color group share ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 784.296pt, "similar characteristics. ")
]

