  #set text(font: "Palatino Linotype", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(187.73pt, 102.26pt, "Figure 10 shows the Image Viewer widget, which was used to display the results of ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 115.1pt, "hierarchical clustering. ")
  #set text(font: "Palatino Linotype", size: 9pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(166.49pt, 229.22pt, "Figure 10. ")
  #set text(font: "Palatino Linotype", size: 9pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(208.85pt, 229.22pt, "Image Viewer used to display results of hierarchical clustering. ")
  #set text(font: "Palatino Linotype", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(187.73pt, 253.7pt, "By carrying out both procedures for recognizing damage in wind turbine blades, it is ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 266.57pt, "observed that the hierarchical clustering model performed better than the logistic regres-")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 279.29pt, "sion model, as it grouped the images more effectively with fewer computational resources. ")
  #set text(font: "Palatino Linotype", size: 9.96pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(166.49pt, 304.13pt, "4. Discussion ")
  #set text(font: "Palatino Linotype", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(187.73pt, 319.97pt, "This study presents advancements in fault detection methodologies for wind turbine ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 332.81pt, "blades, a critical component in the wind energy sector [50]. Given the increasing reliance ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 345.65pt, "on wind power as a sustainable energy source, the operational efficiency and lifespan of ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 358.37pt, "wind turbines have become paramount. Wind turbine blades, exposed to adverse envi-")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 371.21pt, "ronmental conditions and dynamic mechanical loads, are particularly susceptible to a ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 384.05pt, "range of faults that can significantly impact energy production efficiency. Therefore, early ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 396.89pt, "detection of such faults is essential for maintaining system reliability, reducing downtime, ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 409.73pt, "and minimizing maintenance costs. ")
  #line-at(187.73pt, 422.45pt, "The study’s dual-model approach, employing both logistic regression and clustering ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 435.29pt, "techniques, offers a novel perspective on fault detection, contrasting with the predomi-")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 448.15pt, "nantly supervised methods reported in existing literature. The performance of logistic re-")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 460.99pt, "gression, surpassing that of neural networks, decision trees, and naive Bayes in this con-")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 473.83pt, "text, challenges the prevailing assumption that more complex models inherently provide ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 486.55pt, "better results in fault detection scenarios. This finding aligns with recent trends in machine ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 499.39pt, "learning, where simpler models are sometimes preferred for their interpretability and ef-")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 512.23pt, "ficiency, particularly when data characteristics do not support more intricate architec-")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 525.07pt, "tures. ")
  #line-at(187.73pt, 537.91pt, "The superior performance of the clustering model in data segmentation highlights ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 550.63pt, "the potential of unsupervised learning techniques to capture the underlying patterns of ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 563.47pt, "faults in the blades. This result is particularly significant as it suggests that traditional ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 576.31pt, "supervised methods may overlook certain fault patterns that become more apparent when ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 589.15pt, "data are analyzed without predefined labels. The study contributes to the growing body ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 601.99pt, "of work exploring the effectiveness of clustering in industrial applications, particularly in ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 614.71pt, "cases where labeled data are scarce or costly to obtain. ")
  #line-at(187.73pt, 627.58pt, "The use of Orange Data Mining as a practical tool for implementing these models ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 640.42pt, "underscores the accessibility of advanced computational learning techniques. The ability ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 653.26pt, "to leverage such user-friendly platforms without sacrificing analytical rigor opens the ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 666.1pt, "door for broader adoption of these methodologies in the industry. This democratization ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 678.94pt, "of data science tools is crucial for smaller organizations or those with limited resources, ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 691.66pt, "which can benefit from sophisticated fault detection systems without the need for exten-")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 704.5pt, "sive computational infrastructure or specialized expertise. ")
  #line-at(187.73pt, 717.34pt, "The findings suggest that clustering-based models, due to their capacity to discern ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 730.18pt, "subtle fault patterns, may be more effective in environments where data heterogeneity is ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 743.016pt, "high. However, the study also raises important questions about the balance between ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 755.736pt, "model complexity and interpretability, especially in critical applications such as wind tur-")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 768.576pt, "bine maintenance where the stakes are high. ")
]

