#original-page(595.32pt, 841.92pt, (image("graphics/page-18.png", width: 526.5pt), 34.5pt, 67.5pt))[
  #set text(font: "Palatino Linotype", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(36pt, 59.4pt, "Appl. Sci. ")
  #set text(font: "Palatino Linotype", size: 8.04pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(69.984pt, 59.4pt, "2024")
  #set text(font: "Palatino Linotype", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(86.064pt, 59.4pt, ",")
  #set text(font: "Palatino Linotype", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(87.984pt, 59.4pt, " 14")
  #set text(font: "Palatino Linotype", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(98.064pt, 59.4pt, ", x FOR PEER REVIEW ")
  #line-at(528.36pt, 59.4pt, "18 of 21 ")
  #set text(font: "Palatino Linotype", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(187.73pt, 102.26pt, "While the study successfully demonstrates the utility of both logistic regression and ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 115.1pt, "clustering in fault detection, several challenges remain. The performance of these models ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 127.94pt, "in real-world scenarios, where data quality and availability can vary significantly, war-")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 140.66pt, "rants further investigation. Additionally, integrating these models into existing supervi-")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 153.5pt, "sory control and data acquisition (SCADA) systems presents both technical and logistical ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 166.34pt, "challenges that must be addressed for practical implementation. ")
  #line-at(187.73pt, 179.18pt, "Future research could focus on hybrid approaches that combine the strengths of both ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 192.02pt, "supervised and unsupervised learning. For instance, semi-supervised learning techniques ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 204.74pt, "could be explored to leverage available labeled data while also capturing the unstructured ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 217.58pt, "patterns detected by clustering. Furthermore, the study’s methodology could be extended ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 230.42pt, "to other components of wind turbines, such as gearboxes or generators, where similar ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 243.26pt, "fault detection challenges exist. ")
  #set text(font: "Palatino Linotype", size: 9.96pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(166.49pt, 268.13pt, "5. Conclusions ")
  #set text(font: "Palatino Linotype", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(187.73pt, 283.85pt, "The methodology proposed in this study for detecting faults in wind turbine blades ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 296.69pt, "using computational learning techniques has proven to be both effective and robust. The ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 309.53pt, "use of logistic regression as part of the first model outperformed neural networks, decision ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 322.37pt, "trees, and the naive Bayes method, highlighting its value as a tool for identifying patterns ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 335.21pt, "associated with faults. However, the clustering approach implemented in the second ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 347.93pt, "model demonstrated notable superiority in both precision and data segmentation capa-")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 360.77pt, "bility, suggesting that clustering can better capture the underlying characteristics of the ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 373.61pt, "data compared to supervised methods. ")
  #line-at(187.73pt, 386.45pt, "These findings underscore the importance of considering multiple approaches within ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 399.29pt, "computational learning for fault detection in complex systems such as wind turbine ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 412.01pt, "blades. The methodology presented not only offers a new perspective on early fault iden-")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 424.85pt, "tification but also emphasizes the utility of accessible and flexible tools like Orange Data ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 437.69pt, "Mining for implementing advanced solutions in the wind energy industry. Future re-")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 450.55pt, "search could focus on the combination of these methods to further enhance the accuracy ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 463.39pt, "and efficiency of the detection system, as well as on applying these techniques to other ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 476.11pt, "critical components within the energy infrastructure. ")
  #line-at(187.73pt, 488.95pt, "Further work is required to combine methods and apply these techniques to other ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 501.79pt, "critical components in energy infrastructure, such as hybrid modeling approaches and the ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 514.63pt, "combination of different models, including neural networks, decision trees, and logistic ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 527.47pt, "regression, into an ensemble approach such as stacking, bagging, or boosting. This could ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 540.19pt, "enhance predictive performance. Additionally, the implementation of a voting mecha-")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 553.03pt, "nism, whereby the predictions of multiple models are combined to arrive at a final deci-")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 565.87pt, "sion, has the potential to enhance the accuracy of the process. The models could be as-")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 578.71pt, "signed weights based on their performance on specific classes, such as Blade 2 in this ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 591.55pt, "study. Furthermore, multiple neural networks with varied architectures or training data ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 604.39pt, "subsets could be combined. Techniques such as dropout could also be employed to create ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 617.11pt, "an ensemble effect within a single neural network model. The application of pre-trained ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 629.98pt, "models from similar domains and fine-tuning of this specific problem could facilitate ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 642.82pt, "model development and enhance accuracy, particularly in cases with limited data. Addi-")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 655.66pt, "tionally, the exploration of advanced feature engineering techniques to create more dis-")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 668.5pt, "criminative features could assist in improving the model’s performance. Techniques such ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 681.22pt, "as principal component analysis (PCA) for dimensionality reduction or the utilization of ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 694.06pt, "domain knowledge to engineer novel features pertinent to blade failures may prove ben-")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 706.9pt, "eficial. The development of techniques to detect outliers or anomalies that may indicate ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 719.74pt, "the early signs of failure could serve to enhance the efficacy of the classification models. ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 732.58pt, "Anomalies may be identified through the utilization of clustering techniques, statistical ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 745.296pt, "methods, or specialized models such as autoencoders. Furthermore, the techniques ex-")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 758.136pt, "plored herein could be adapted for the prediction of failures in other critical components, ")
  #line-at(166.49pt, 770.976pt, "including wind turbine blades and solar panel systems. These components exhibit ")
]

